  "question": {
    "text": "Two masses&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> connected with an inextensible&nbsp;string of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math>&nbsp;lie on a smooth horizontal plane.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is given a velocity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> along the ground perpendicular to line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi></math> as shown in the figure. Find the tension in a string during their subsequence motion.<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0007_a16a9ebc0fc6.jpg\" style=\"width: 186px; height: 221px;\" />"
